$Ibo ="TERMS AND CONDITIONS";
$Ibo_sub = "Effective Date: March 15, 2022";
$Ibo_text_01 ="PLEASE READ THIS IBO AGREEMENT CAREFULLY. THIS IBO AGREEMENT REQUIRES THE USE OF INDIVIDUAL ARBITRATION TO RESOLVE DISPUTES, INSTEAD OF JURY TRIALS OR CLASS ACTIONS, AND ALSO LIMITS THE REMEDIES AVAILABLE TO YOU IN THE EVENT OF A DISPUTE.";

$Ibo_01 ='By applying to become an EVO Global IBO through the EVO Global website and the online enrollment process, I acknowledge and agree that I have read and understood the EVO Global IBO Agreement, which consists of these Terms and Conditions, the EVO Global Policies and Procedures, the EVO Global Compensation Plan, and the EVO Global Social Media Policy ("IBO Agreement"). I confirm that my name and contact information are correct, that I am of legal age to enter into the IBO Agreement, and that I wish to become an IBO. I agree to comply with the terms and conditions set forth in the IBO Agreement. I understand that the IBO Agreement between me and EVO MOVEMENT INTERNATIONAL S.A. de C.V. ("EVO Global") will become effective only upon EVO Global’s acceptance of my completed online IBO application and EVO Global’s receipt of my Initial and Recurring Fees. I understand that EVO Global has the right to accept or reject my application at its sole discretion.';
$Ibo_02 ='I understand that there is no requirement to become an IBO beyond entering into the IBO Agreement and paying the Initial and Recurring Fees. Recurring Fees are due every twenty-eight (28) days ("Recurring Fees"). No other purchase of sales materials, IBO training materials, or EVO Global Products and/or Services is required, and any such purchase by me is strictly voluntary. I understand that commissions, bonuses, or other compensation I may earn as an IBO ("Compensation") and rank advancement are based solely on the successful sale of EVO Global Products and/or Services to customers, and that I am not required to purchase any EVO Global Product and/or Service.';
$Ibo_03 ='I understand that no Compensation is earned for enrolling new IBOs and that I will only be compensated based on the activities of other IBOs to the extent of sales of EVO Global Products and/or Services to customers by such IBOs.';
$Ibo_04 ='I hereby authorize EVO Global to (i) charge the initial fee and first recurring fee to my credit or debit card on file with EVO Global or another selected payment method (the "Payment Method"); and (ii) automatically charge the Payment Method for each Recurring Fee payment due and payable under this IBO Agreement. I agree to ensure that the Payment Method remains valid at all times and to provide EVO Global with all necessary information to enable EVO Global to charge the Payment Method for all amounts owed and payable by me to EVO Global. If the Payment Method expires or becomes invalid for any reason, or if I fail to pay fees when due, my IBO position will be deactivated, and at EVO Global’s option this IBO Agreement will terminate, and I will forfeit all rights under this IBO Agreement. EVO Global may, at its discretion, choose to keep my account open in a deactivated status. I understand and agree that if I pay using digital currency, my payment may be processed by a blockchain payment processor chosen by EVO Global on its behalf.';
$Ibo_05 ='If I enter into this IBO Agreement on behalf of a corporation, limited liability company, partnership, trust, or other entity, I represent that I have the authority to enter into such agreements on behalf of the entity and understand that the IBO Agreement will be conditioned upon EVO Global’s receipt of documentation verifying the identity of the entity’s owners and officers.';
$Ibo_06 ='This IBO Agreement will continue unless and until terminated earlier as permitted under this IBO Agreement. I agree that EVO Global may from time to time modify the initial and recurring fees by written notice delivered by email and/or posted in the EVO Global Center in my back office.';
$Ibo_07 ='The provisions of this IBO Agreement which by their nature are intended to survive the termination of this IBO Agreement shall survive termination, including but not limited to the Dispute Resolution Provisions, restrictive covenants, and all provisions relating to indemnification, confidentiality, and data protection.';
$Ibo_08 ='I agree that I am an independent contractor for all purposes under applicable federal, state, and local statutes, rules, regulations, and other laws ("Applicable Law"), and I am not an employee, partner, agent, franchisee, or legal representative of EVO Global, nor may I represent myself as such. I am responsible for my own business and am free to select my own means, methods, and manner of operation, and free to choose the time and place of my activities as an IBO. If I hire individuals to perform services for my independent business, I understand that I am responsible for their acts and omissions and for ensuring their compliance with this IBO Agreement and Applicable Law. I understand that I am solely responsible for filing and remitting any taxes and obtaining any licenses, permits, authorizations, or insurance required to conduct my IBO business. I will have no power or authority to bind EVO Global in any way, directly or indirectly, and I am not entitled to vacation, holidays, disability, insurance, pensions, retirement plans, or any other benefits offered or provided by EVO Global to its employees.';
$Ibo_09 ='I may terminate this IBO Agreement for any reason, at any time, by providing written notice to EVO Global at support@evoglobal.online. EVO Global may terminate this IBO Agreement in accordance with EVO Global’s Policies and Procedures or by giving me written notice if I breach any part of this IBO Agreement.';
$Ibo_10 ='I acknowledge that no income, benefits, or success are guaranteed, and that I will not make any claims of guaranteed benefits or representations of expected earnings as an IBO.';
$Ibo_11 ='I understand that EVO Global may charge a fee to process all Compensation. Compensation will be paid to the Payment Method I choose in my virtual office. If I wish to change the Payment Method for receiving Compensation, I understand that EVO Global may charge a fee to administer such change. Furthermore, I acknowledge and agree that any payment EVO Global issues or transfers to my e-wallet and which I do not request or which remains unclaimed for three (3) months after the date of issuance (“Unclaimed Funds”) will be returned to EVO Global and held by EVO Global in an account, and that EVO Global may assess a $10 per month account maintenance fee (the “Account Maintenance Fee”) until I have claimed all Unclaimed Funds held by EVO Global. I acknowledge and understand that EVO Global may deduct the Account Maintenance Fee every twenty-eight (28) days from the Unclaimed Funds, and if there are insufficient Unclaimed Funds held by EVO Global from which to deduct the Account Maintenance Fee when due, then the Account Maintenance Fee will be prorated to reflect the remaining Unclaimed Funds, and the remaining due Account Maintenance Fee will be charged to the Payment Method. When no Unclaimed Funds are owed to me by EVO Global, the account will be closed. Additionally, I acknowledge that Unclaimed Funds may be subject to applicable escheatment laws which may require EVO Global to deliver all or part of the Unclaimed Funds to the appropriate state or government authority.';
$Ibo_12 ='Compensation Payment in Cryptocurrency. Unless otherwise agreed with the Company, if I choose to receive my Compensation in cryptocurrency, I understand that I am solely responsible for opening, securing, and maintaining my wallet (“Wallet”). My “Wallet” means the location, wallet, address, account, or storage device I designate as the place where the cryptocurrency to be delivered to me should be sent. I acknowledge that the transfer and payment of Compensation in the form of cryptocurrency is complete once the cryptocurrency has been successfully delivered to my Wallet, and that once the Company transfers the cryptocurrency, it belongs to me and is under my exclusive control. I will bear all risk of loss of the cryptocurrency, including but not limited to loss resulting from unauthorized access to my Wallet, fraud, or theft. I acknowledge that the value of cryptocurrency may be volatile, and that the value of the cryptocurrency I receive and/or the amount of funding may be different (higher or lower) than the fair market value or other measure of cryptocurrency value at the time of payment by EVO Global. I will bear all risk of loss resulting from converting cryptocurrency into any other currency and will be responsible for all transaction fees arising from the transfer and payment of Compensation in cryptocurrency. I agree to indemnify and hold harmless the Company and its affiliates, and their respective officers, directors, employees, and agents, from and against any loss, damage, liability, or expense, including reasonable costs and attorneys’ fees and expenses, arising from or related to the terms of this Agreement.';
$Ibo_13 ='I will comply with EVO Global’s Policies and Procedures. I also agree not to engage in or carry out deceptive, fraudulent, or unethical practices, nor make false or misleading statements, regarding EVO Global, EVO Global’s Products and/or Services, and the EVO Global business opportunity.';
$Ibo_14 ='I agree to comply with Applicable Law governing the marketing, sale, or promotion of EVO Global’s Products and/or Services. I understand that EVO Global offers educational Products and/or Services, and that at no time will I claim or imply, directly or indirectly, that EVO Global offers financial advice or services, or investment advice, or acts as a regulated intermediary.';
$Ibo_15 ='I understand that if EVO Global has reason to believe I have breached the terms of the IBO Agreement, EVO Global may suspend my IBO position to investigate the alleged violation and any Compensation that may be owed to me may be withheld by EVO Global until a final resolution is reached. I acknowledge that if EVO Global determines I have violated this IBO Agreement, then EVO Global may, at its option, (if permitted by applicable law) impose fines which may be withheld from commissions owed to me and/or terminate this IBO Agreement, in which case I will not be entitled to any Compensation of any kind.';
$Ibo_16 ='I acknowledge and understand that EVO Global reserves the right to vary or change the terms and conditions of the EVO Global Compensation Plan at any time, including without limitation those terms and conditions relating to eligibility. Furthermore, I acknowledge and understand that EVO Global may also offer me from time to time certain incentives outside of the EVO Global Compensation Plan (e.g., promotional incentives), and that such incentives may be subject to separate terms and conditions.';
$Ibo_17 ='I agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless EVO Global and its shareholders, directors, officers, contractors, and employees from and against any claims, damages, costs, and expenses, including without limitation attorneys’ fees and costs, arising out of or in connection with my actions or omissions in performance of this IBO Agreement.';
$Ibo_18 ='IN NO EVENT SHALL EVO GLOBAL BE LIABLE FOR INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL, SPECIAL, PUNITIVE, OR INCIDENTAL DAMAGES (INCLUDING WITHOUT LIMITATION DAMAGES FOR LOSS OF BUSINESS PROFITS, BUSINESS INTERRUPTION, AND THE LIKE) ARISING OUT OF OR IN CONNECTION WITH ANY CAUSE, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO ANY BREACH OF WARRANTY OR ANY DELAY, ACT, ERROR, OR OMISSION OF EVO GLOBAL OR THE DELIVERY, NON-DELIVERY, DISCONTINUATION, OR MODIFICATION OF ANY PRODUCT OR SERVICE BY EVO GLOBAL, EVEN IF EVO GLOBAL HAS BEEN ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.';
$Ibo_19 ='DISPUTE RESOLUTION PLEASE READ THIS SECTION OF THE IBO AGREEMENT CAREFULLY, AS IT PROVIDES FOR RESOLUTION OF MOST DISPUTES THROUGH BINDING ARBITRATION AND INCLUDES CERTAIN WAIVERS, INCLUDING WAIVERS OF CLASS ACTIONS, CLASS ARBITRATION, AND JURY TRIAL.';

$Ibo_text_02='All disputes and claims relating to EVO Global, the IBO Agreement, or EVO Global’s Products and/or Services, the rights and obligations of an IBO and EVO Global, or any other claim or cause of action relating to the performance of an IBO and EVO Global under the IBO Agreement (“Dispute”) shall be fully and finally resolved by arbitration in Cancun, Quintana Roo, Mexico, or at another location prescribed by EVO Global, in accordance with Mexican Law. The arbitrator’s decision shall be final and binding on the parties and may, if necessary, be reduced to judgment in any court of competent jurisdiction. Each party to the arbitration shall be responsible for its own costs and arbitration expenses, including legal and filing fees. Nothing in the IBO Agreement shall prevent EVO Global from seeking and obtaining from any court with jurisdiction an attachment order, temporary, preliminary, or permanent injunction, or other available remedy to safeguard and protect EVO Global’s interest before, during, or after the filing of any arbitration or other proceeding pending a decision or award in connection with any arbitration or other proceeding. For the avoidance of doubt, claims by different IBOs shall be heard in separate, bilateral arbitration proceedings. The arbitration proceedings and any award shall be kept confidential. No amendment to this arbitration provision shall apply to a Dispute of which EVO Global had actual knowledge as of the amendment date. Any termination of this arbitration provision shall not be effective until 10 days after reasonable notice of termination has been given to IBOs or as to Disputes that arose before the termination date.
CLASS ACTION WAIVER. IN THE EVENT ANY DISPUTE PROCEEDS IN COURT RATHER THAN THROUGH ARBITRATION, FOR ANY REASON, EACH OF THE IBO AND EVO GLOBAL AGREE THAT SUCH DISPUTE SHALL ONLY BE RESOLVED ON AN INDIVIDUAL BASIS. EACH OF THE IBO AND EVO GLOBAL SPECIFICALLY AGREE THAT CLAIMS MAY BE BROUGHT AGAINST THE OTHER ONLY IN THEIR INDIVIDUAL CAPACITY, AND NOT AS A PLAINTIFF OR CLASS MEMBER IN ANY PURPORTED CLASS, COLLECTIVE, REPRESENTATIVE, OR GROUP ACTION.
JURY TRIAL WAIVER. TO THE EXTENT ANY DISPUTE PROCEEDS IN COURT RATHER THAN THROUGH ARBITRATION, FOR ANY REASON, IF NOT PROHIBITED BY APPLICABLE LAW, EACH OF THE IBO AND EVO GLOBAL HEREBY WAIVE ANY RIGHT TO A JURY TRIAL TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW.
Delegation to Arbitrator. Except as provided in this Section 19, I acknowledge and agree that the arbitrator(s), and not any federal, state, or local court, shall have the exclusive authority to resolve any Dispute relating to the interpretation, enforceability, or validity of these Dispute Resolution Provisions, including without limitation any claim that these Dispute Resolution Provisions are void or voidable.
Severability. If any provision contained in these Dispute Resolution Provisions is found invalid or unenforceable, such provision shall automatically be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make the parties’ agreement to arbitrate valid and enforceable. If a provision conflicts with a mandatory provision of Applicable Law, the conflicting provision shall be automatically severed, and the remainder shall be interpreted to incorporate the mandatory provision. In the event of such severance or modification, the remainder shall not be affected.
Termination. The Dispute Resolution Provisions shall remain in effect even after termination of the IBO Agreement or termination of the IBO’s business relationship with EVO Global.';

$Ibo_20='RESTRICTIVE COVENANTS';

$Ibo_20_01 ='For the purposes of this Agreement and this Section 20, the following terms shall have the meanings set forth below: “EVO Global Products and/or Services” means all digital educational products and online educational training and instructional services EVO Global offers for sale from time to time.
“Customer/Member” means any person or entity that purchases EVO Global Products and/or Services. “Downline” means all IBOs who are on the first level or below your IBO position in your IBO sales organization.
“Participating Party” means a shareholder, partner, or beneficial owner of an IBO position holding an interest in the IBO position equal to or greater than five percent (5%) of the total interest therein, or any individual acquiring Customers/Members or recruiting prospective IBOs in connection with an IBO position as permitted by the IBO Agreement. “Restricted IBO” means any individual who is or, within the last six (6) months, has been, a party (directly or as a Participating Party) to an IBO Agreement with EVO Global. “Solicit” means, in effect or by intent, to solicit, recruit, enroll, sponsor, attract, induce, influence, or encourage, in each case in any manner and through any medium or method (including, without limitation, communications made affirmatively or responsively, directly or indirectly, expressly or impliedly, or personally or through or with one or more third parties). “Solicitation” means any activity that constitutes Soliciting, including but not limited to personal meetings, phone calls (e.g., direct calls and three-way calls), emails, text messages, chat messages, and social media posts.
';

$Ibo_20_02 ='Non-Solicitation of Customers/Members. During the term of this IBO Agreement and for a period of one (1) year following its expiration or early termination, I agree that I will not Solicit any Customer/Member to whom I marketed EVO Global Products and/or Services within the two (2) years immediately prior to (i) move their business away from EVO Global; or (ii) purchase products or services that are the same as or similar to any EVO Global Product and/or Service, unless expressly approved in writing by EVO Global. I acknowledge and agree that all Customers/Members Solicited by an IBO for the promotion or sale of EVO Global Products and/or Services shall be deemed Customers/Members of EVO Global and not of the IBO, regardless of whether the IBO originally introduced such Customer/Member to EVO Global.';
$Ibo_20_03 ='Non-Solicitation of Restricted IBOs. During the term of this IBO Agreement and for a period of one (1) year following its expiration or early termination, I agree that I will not Solicit any Restricted IBO to participate, personally or through any entity or other means, in another network marketing, multilevel marketing, or direct sales business opportunity. I acknowledge and agree that due to the nature of network marketing it is reasonable for the foregoing prohibition on Solicitation to extend to all markets where EVO Global conducts business.
D. Survival of Restrictive Covenants. I acknowledge and agree that my obligations under this Section 20 shall survive the expiration or termination of this IBO Agreement for any reason. Furthermore, I acknowledge and agree that temporary and permanent injunctive relief is an appropriate remedy to prevent further harm to EVO Global from my violation of the provisions of this Section 20.';

$Ibo_21='This IBO Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the law of the State of Quintana Roo, Mexico, without regard to conflict of laws principles. The parties consent to jurisdiction and venue before any federal or state court in Cancun, Quintana Roo, for purposes of enforcing an arbitrator’s award or any other matter not subject to arbitration.';
$Ibo_22="I acknowledge that EVO Global fully reserves the right to amend or modify this IBO Agreement at any time by notifying me of the changes by email or posting the revisions on the EVO Global website or in the EVO Global virtual office (my.evoglobal.life), Any change to this IBO Agreement may be made effective at EVO Global's discretion on the execution date, on the date of publication of the amended IBO Agreement by EVO Global, or prospectively on a date specified in the amendment. This IBO Agreement may not be modified or amended except as described herein, and no amendment shall apply retroactively.";

$Ibo_23 = "The IBO Agreement constitutes the complete agreement and understanding between me and EVO Global regarding its subject matter and supersedes any prior or contemporaneous agreements, representations, commitments, or understandings, whether oral or written, made by or between EVO Global and me. In the event of a conflict between the terms and conditions contained in the IBO Agreement, the following order of precedence shall apply: first, (i) the Dispute Resolution Provisions, then (ii) these Terms and Conditions, then (iii) EVO Global Policies and Procedures, and finally (iv) the EVO Global Compensation Plan.";

$Ibo_24 = "I understand that I may not assign this IBO Agreement, or any part of it, or any of the duties, obligations, or responsibilities contained herein, without the prior written consent of EVO Global, which may be withheld, conditioned, or delayed at EVO Global's sole discretion. EVO Global may assign this IBO Agreement at any time without my consent, and upon doing so, EVO Global shall be released from any duties, obligations, and/or liabilities arising from this IBO Agreement. This IBO Agreement shall be binding upon and inure to the benefit of the heirs, successors, and permitted assigns of the parties hereto.";

$Ibo_25 = "Subject to the Dispute Resolution Provisions, if any provision of this IBO Agreement is determined by a competent authority to be invalid or unenforceable in whole or in part for any reason, the validity of the remaining provisions or parts thereof shall not be affected, and such authority shall reform the IBO Agreement to the extent necessary in a manner that most closely expresses the intent of the invalid or unenforceable provision while making enforceable the provision or part thereof that would otherwise be unenforceable.";

$Ibo_text_03 = "CANCELLATION NOTICE";

$Ibo_text_03_01 = "Unless otherwise required by applicable law, I may cancel this transaction without penalty or obligation and receive a full refund if I submit a valid cancellation notice postmarked within seven (7) days from the date of this IBO Agreement, not including the signature date. I understand that, unless otherwise required by applicable law, if I cancel after the seven (7) day period, I am not entitled to any refund. To cancel this IBO Agreement, I must submit a written and dated copy of the cancellation notice by email or through my virtual office. Alternatively, I may deliver the cancellation notice in writing to the following address: Calle Buenavista 31 int 4, Colonia Barrio del Niño Jesús, Mexico City, Mexico. Some jurisdictions require a longer cancellation period by law, and where applicable cancellation law conflicts with EVO Global's policy, such law shall prevail and the cancellation rights set forth herein shall be deemed modified to reflect the applicable requirements.";

$Politics_01 = "STATEMENT OF POLICIES AND PROCEDURES";
$Politics_intro = "Introduction";
$Politics_text_01 = "1.1 EVO Global Policies and Procedures and Compensation Plan Incorporated into the IBO Agreement. The term 'Agreement' or 'IBO Agreement' collectively refers to the online application, electronic signature process, the Terms and Conditions of the IBO Agreement, these Policies and Procedures, the IBO Social Media Policy, the Compensation Plan, and any other guidelines that may be implemented from time to time, including any modifications thereto.
1.2 Statement of Mutual Commitment. Evo Movement International S.A. de C.V. (hereinafter referred to as 'EVO Global') recognizes the importance of maintaining a long-term and mutually beneficial relationship with its independent business owners ('IBOs'). EVO Global expects its IBOs to conduct themselves in a professional, honest, and considerate manner, comply with all applicable laws and regulations, present information about EVO Global and its services accurately, and support and protect the integrity of EVO Global's income opportunity.
1.3 Code of Ethics (a) EVO Global's Code of Ethics provides: (i) An IBO must show fairness, tolerance, and respect to all individuals associated with EVO Global, regardless of race, gender, social class, or religion, fostering a positive teamwork environment, goodwill, and community spirit; (ii) An IBO must strive to resolve business issues, including situations and disputes with other IBOs, emphasizing tact, sensitivity, and goodwill, taking care not to create additional problems; (iii) IBOs must be honest, responsible, professional, and conduct themselves with integrity; (iv) IBOs must not make disparaging statements about EVO Global, other IBOs, officers, employees, contractors, suppliers, or agents of EVO Global, its services, strategies, sales and marketing campaigns, or the Compensation Plan, or make statements that unreasonably offend, mislead, or coerce others; (v) IBOs must represent EVO Global's services solely as an educational and informational platform and service and under no circumstances should an IBO represent that EVO Global, any IBO, or EVO Global educator provides investment or trading advice or is affiliated with a broker or investment advisor; (vi) IBOs must not recommend brokers or investment advisors to EVO Global clients or other IBOs.
(b) EVO Global may take appropriate action against an IBO if, at its sole and absolute discretion, it determines that the IBO's conduct is harmful, disruptive, or damaging to EVO Global or other IBOs.
(c) Negative and disparaging comments about EVO Global, its services, strategies, the Agreement, or Compensation Plan, made to EVO Global, in the field, or at any EVO Global meeting and/or event, or disruptive behavior at any meeting and/or event, have no purpose other than to diminish the enthusiasm of other IBOs and clients. IBOs must not disparage, denigrate, or speak negatively about EVO Global, fellow IBOs, EVO Global services or strategies, the Compensation Plan, or any director, officer, employee, contractor, supplier, or agent of EVO Global. Such conduct represents a material breach of the Agreement and may be subject to penalties as deemed appropriate by EVO Global.
1.4 Purpose of Policies and Procedures (a) EVO Global is a subscription-based, direct-to-consumer education and training company that markets its services and strategies through a network of IBOs. To clearly define the relationship between IBOs and EVO Global and explicitly establish a standard for acceptable business conduct, EVO Global has established the Agreement, including these Policies and Procedures.
(b) IBOs are required to comply with all terms and conditions set forth in the Agreement, which EVO Global may modify from time to time at its sole and absolute discretion in accordance with the terms herein; and all federal, state, and/or local laws governing their EVO Global business.
(c) IBOs must carefully review the information in the Agreement, including these Policies and Procedures. If an IBO has any questions regarding a policy, rule, or guideline, they are encouraged to seek an answer from the Company's FAQ, found in the IBO virtual office, their personal Sponsor, or EVO Global Customer Service Team.
(d) It is the Sponsor's responsibility to provide the most current version of the Agreement, including these Policies and Procedures, the Income Disclosure Statement, EVO Global Compensation Plan, and all social media or other guidelines, including any amendments thereto, to their downline IBOs.
1.5 Changes, Amendments, and Modifications 
(a) As applicable laws and the business environment change periodically, EVO Global reserves the right to modify the Agreement and service prices at its sole and absolute discretion.
(b) Any amendment, change, or modification shall be effective immediately and without prior notice, and may be communicated through one of the following methods:
i. Posting in the IBO virtual office and EVO Global official website;
ii. Email;
iii. Any EVO Global communication channel or social media (e.g., Facebook, Instagram, Twitter, and/or the EVO Global App).";

$Politics_02 ='2.0 BASIC PRINCIPLES';
$Politics_02_01 ='2.1 Becoming an IBO';
$Politics_02_01_text ='To become an IBO, an applicant must meet the following requirements: (i) Be of legal age (not a minor) in the applicant’s country, state, province, or territory of residence and be at least 18 years old. (ii) Reside or have a valid address in a country where EVO Global operates its business. (iii) Have a valid tax identification number. (iv) Provide a verified mobile phone number or email address that is not in use or associated with any other EVO Global account.';

$Politics_02_02 ='2.2 New IBO Registration';
$Politics_02_02_text ='(a) A potential new IBO may self-enroll on any IBO or EVO Global Sponsor replicated website by entering their personal information and accepting the terms of the Agreement. (b) If an applicant enrolls by creating an account listing a certain Sponsor and subsequently enrolls a second time listing multiple Sponsors, only the first completed form received by EVO Global will be accepted. EVO Global reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to make the final decision regarding all such registrations.';

$Politics_03 ='3.0 EVO GLOBAL IBO RESPONSIBILITIES';
$Politics_03_01 ='3.1 Accurate IBO Information';
$Politics_03_01_text ='(a) It is the responsibility of the IBO to ensure that EVO Global has the correct contact information for all correspondence and in the IBO account profile. (b) An IBO must allow up to seventy-two (72) hours for processing after any changes to the IBO account profile have been received by the EVO Global Support Team.';

$Politics_03_02 ='3.2 Training and Leadership';
$Politics_03_02_text ='(a) Any IBO sponsoring another IBO in EVO Global must perform an authentic assistance and training role to ensure that the IBO’s sales and marketing organization operates the IBO’s EVO Global business correctly. Sponsoring IBOs must maintain ongoing contact and communication with the IBOs in their sales and marketing organizations. (b) A Sponsor IBO must support, educate, and mentor IBOs in their sales and marketing organization to ensure that IBOs do not make improper business claims or engage in illegal or inappropriate conduct. (c) Sponsor IBOs are encouraged to educate and train new IBOs on EVO Global services and strategies, effective sales techniques, the EVO Global Compensation Plan, compliance with the Agreement, and any social media guidelines or any other guidelines and amendments implemented at that time. (d) EVO Global emphasizes and encourages all IBOs to sell EVO Global services and strategies to Clients. IBOs receive compensation only for sales to Clients. (e) Use of sales and marketing materials. To promote the services, strategies, and opportunities offered by EVO Global, IBOs must use the sales and marketing materials provided by EVO Global. All IBOs must safeguard and promote the good reputation of EVO Global and its services and strategies.';

$Politics_03_03 ='3.3 Sponsorship';
$Politics_03_03_text ='(a) A Sponsor introduces IBOs or Clients to EVO Global, assists them in completing their enrollment, and supports and trains those in their sales and marketing organization. (b) EVO Global recognizes the Sponsor as the name(s) listed on the first online IBO application submitted to EVO Global. (c) EVO Global acknowledges that each new prospect has the right to ultimately choose their own Sponsor, but EVO Global will not allow IBOs to engage in unethical sponsorship activities.';

$Politics_03_04 ='3.4 Unethical Sponsorship';
$Politics_03_04_text ='(a) Unethical sponsorship activities include, but are not limited to, soliciting, offering, or participating in unhealthy competition by attempting to acquire a prospect or new IBO from a fellow IBO or influencing another IBO to transfer to a different Sponsor. (b) Reports of unethical sponsorship must be submitted in writing to the EVO Global Compliance Team within the first thirty (30) days of a new IBO enrollment. (c) EVO Global prohibits the act of “Stacking.” Stacking is the unauthorized manipulation of EVO Global’s marketing system and/or Compensation Plan to trigger commissions or cause the promotion of a direct or indirect IBO in their sales and marketing organization in an unearned manner. (d) If IBOs participate in soliciting and/or attracting members from another direct selling company to sell or distribute EVO Global services or strategies, such IBOs risk legal action from the other company.';

$Politics_03_05 ='3.5 Prohibition on Cross-Sponsoring/Recruitment';
$Politics_03_05_text ='(a) For the purposes of this section, “Cross-Sponsoring” or “Cross-Recruiting” is defined as enrolling an individual or Business Entity in a different sponsorship line who already has a signed IBO Agreement. Actual or attempted Cross-Sponsoring is not allowed. If EVO Global verifies Cross-Sponsoring, penalties up to and including termination of the IBO’s position may be imposed. (b) Recruiting EVO Global members into an IBO’s organization may result in suspension, fines, and possible termination. (c) Use of a spouse’s or relative’s name, trade names, aliases, DBA names, corporation, partnership, federal business numbers, or fictitious IDs to evade or circumvent this policy is not permitted. (d) This policy does not prohibit the transfer of an EVO Global business in accordance with the Sale or Transfer Policy set forth in these Policies and Procedures.';

$Politics_03_06 ='3.6 Solicitation for Other Companies or Services';
$Politics_03_06_text ='(a) An IBO may participate in other direct sales, multilevel, network marketing, or relationship marketing businesses, provided they are for non-competing services, strategies, or products. However, during the term of the Agreement and for one (1) year thereafter, an IBO may not solicit or recruit any fellow IBO or Client to whom the IBO has marketed EVO Global services or strategies within the preceding two (2) years for (i) participating, personally or through any entity or other means, in another direct selling, network, or multilevel business opportunity; (ii) transferring their business out of EVO Global; or (iii) purchasing products or services that are the same or similar to any EVO Global service and/or strategy unless expressly approved in writing by EVO Global. (b) For the purposes of this Section, the terms “sponsor” or “recruit” mean soliciting, enrolling, encouraging, or attempting to influence in any way (directly or indirectly) another IBO or Client to enroll or participate in any other direct sales or network marketing opportunity. Such conduct constitutes recruitment even if the IBO’s actions are in response to an inquiry made by another IBO or Client. (c) Due to the nature of network marketing, the parties agree that it is reasonable that the prohibition on prior solicitation extends to all markets in which EVO Global conducts business. (d) All Clients solicited by an IBO for promotion or sale of EVO Global Services and strategies are considered EVO Global Clients, not the IBO’s, whether or not the IBO originally introduced such Client to EVO Global. (e) During the term of this Agreement, IBOs must not sell, or induce others to sell, any competing service or strategy, including training materials, to EVO Global Clients or IBOs. Any product or service in the same category as an EVO Global strategy or service is considered a competitor. (f) An IBO may sell non-competing services or strategies to EVO Global Clients and IBOs personally sponsored. (g) An IBO may not display or bundle EVO Global services or strategies, in sales literature, on a website, social media platforms, or sales meetings, with services, products, or strategies from another business to avoid confusing or misleading a Client or prospective IBO into believing there is a relationship between EVO Global and non-EVO Global services or strategies. (h) An IBO may not offer a non-EVO Global opportunity, strategy, service, or product at any EVO Global meeting, event, seminar, or convention, or immediately after an EVO Global event. (i) An IBO may not be affiliated with a broker or investment advisor and combine or associate EVO Global products, services, or strategies with the services of a broker or investment advisor. (j) Violation of any provisions in this section shall constitute unreasonable and unjustified contractual interference between EVO Global and its IBOs and would cause irreparable harm to EVO Global and its IBOs. In such an event, EVO Global may, at its sole discretion, impose any sanction it deems necessary and appropriate against such IBO or the IBO’s positions, including termination, or seek immediate relief without posting a bond.';

$Politics_04 ='4.0 GENERAL AGREEMENTS AND UNDERSTANDINGS';
$Politics_04_01 ='4.1 Granted Rights';
$Politics_04_01_text ='EVO Global hereby grants the IBO a non-exclusive right, based on the terms and conditions contained in the Agreement, to: (i) Promote and sell EVO Global services and strategies; and (ii) Sponsor new IBOs and Clients in countries where EVO Global currently operates or may operate in the future. No feature of the Compensation Plan constitutes a personal purchase requirement to become an IBO, advance in rank, or fully participate in the Compensation Plan. No one is required to make any purchase at any time to fully participate as an IBO, except for the monthly administrative fee payable for the administrative support of the IBO’s business, the IBO virtual office, and support services.';

$Politics_04_02 ='4.2 IBO Agreement Renewal and Expiration';
$Politics_04_02_text ='If the IBO allows their IBO account to become inactive due to non-payment, the IBO will lose all rights to their downline organization during any inactive period until the IBO reactivates the account. (i) If the former IBO reactivates the account, EVO Global may allow the IBO to resume the rank and position held immediately prior to expiration. However, the paid level of such IBO will not be restored unless the IBO qualifies at that paid level in the new month. The IBO is not eligible to receive commissions for the period the IBO’s position was inactive. (ii) Any IBO who has been terminated or canceled is not eligible to reapply for an EVO Global business for six (6) months after the IBO Agreement expires, except with the express written consent of EVO Global. (iii) The sales and marketing organization of a terminated or canceled IBO account may, at EVO Global’s option, be compressed up to the immediate active IBO in the hierarchy.';

$Politics_04_03 ='4.3 Effect of Cancellation';
$Politics_04_03_text ='After cancellation of an IBO due to voluntary or involuntary termination (collectively, a "Cancellation"), such IBO: (i) Will have no right, title, claim, or interest to any commissions or bonuses from sales generated by the former IBO’s sales and marketing organization or any other payments associated with the former IBO position; (ii) Waives any and all claims to ownership or interest in or to the former IBO’s sales and marketing organization; and (iii) Will receive commissions and bonuses only for the last full pay period in which the IBO was active prior to cancellation, less any amounts withheld during any suspension period or during a pre-involuntary cancellation investigation, and less any other amounts owed to EVO Global.';

$Politics_04_04 ='4.4 Changes to the IBO Account';
$Politics_04_04_text ='(a) An IBO may add a spouse or partner to the account or change the ownership from an individual to a Business Entity by submitting a written request, accompanied by a new completed and signed IBO Agreement by the authorized representatives of the Business Entity and a Business Registration Form, if applicable, and any appropriate supporting documentation. EVO Global reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to accept or reject any such request. (b) EVO Global may impose a $200 fee to process an IBO account change in accordance with these Policies and Procedures.';

$Politics_04_05 ='4.5 Unauthorized Transfer and Re-enrollment';
$Politics_04_05_text ='If an IBO discovers that another IBO in their downline has re-enrolled under a different IBO, the discovering IBO has ninety (90) days from the date the downline IBO enrolled under a new IBO to notify the EVO Global Compliance Team and request the downline IBO be transferred back to the IBO’s downline. After the ninety (90) day period expires, the IBO’s right to claim a new IBO to their downline is forfeited.';

$Politics_04_06 ='4.6 Sponsor or Placement Changes for IBOs';
$Politics_04_06_text ='(a) Location changes/corrections may be requested within ten (10) days from the enrollment date. Such adjustments require a written request addressed to the EVO Global Customer Service Team, sent from the personal office of the Sponsor, as well as the IBO being moved, and in some cases from additional IBOs located above the IBO. (b) Generally, Sponsor changes are not permitted. However, corrections can be made if reported to the EVO Global Compliance Team within twenty-four (24) hours of enrollment. Sponsor corrections must be requested from the original Sponsor’s office and must indicate the reason for the correction. (c) At EVO Global’s sole discretion, IBOs who have been inactive for at least six (6) months, and have not submitted a voluntary termination letter, are eligible to request a transfer to a new Sponsor or Placement of their choice. (d) When an IBO is transferred under this Section 4.6, a new EVO Global ID number will be assigned to the IBO. (e) The transferred IBO does not retain previous rank, downline organization, or commission rights from previous sales and marketing organizations. The existing sales and marketing organization of the transferred IBO remains in its original Sponsor or Placement line. (f) EVO Global reserves the right to correct Sponsor or Placement errors at any time and in any manner it deems necessary.';

$Politics_04_07 ='4.7 Organization Changes';
$Politics_04_07_text ='(a) An IBO may only transfer between EVO Global sales and marketing organizations if they submit a voluntary termination letter to the EVO Global Customer Service Team and remain inactive with, or in, EVO Global for six (6) months from EVO Global’s receipt of the request letter. After six (6) months, the IBO is eligible to re-enroll under a different Sponsor or receive a different Placement. (b) EVO Global reserves the right and discretion to approve or deny any re-enrollment request following an IBO termination. (c) If an IBO re-enrolls after voluntary termination, a new EVO Global ID number will be assigned. The IBO will have no right to retain any previous rank, sales and marketing organization, or commission rights from any previous organization.';

$Politics_04_08 ='4.8 Voluntary Termination';
$Politics_04_08_text ='(a) An IBO may immediately terminate their position by sending written notice or email to the EVO Global Customer Service Team at support@evoglobal.online. The written notice must include the following: (i) The IBO’s intention to terminate their IBO account; (ii) Termination date; (iii) EVO Global Identification Number; and (iv) IBO signature. (b) An IBO may not use termination as a means to immediately change Sponsor and Placement. A voluntarily terminated IBO is not eligible to reapply for a position or have any financial interest in any EVO Global business for six (6) months from the receipt of the written termination notice. They also may not promote EVO Global, represent themselves as affiliated in any way with EVO Global, or attend EVO Global events after termination.';

$Politics_04_09 ='4.9 Involuntary Termination';
$Politics_04_09_text ='(a) EVO Global reserves the right to suspend or terminate an IBO for any reason, including but not limited to: (i) Violation of any term or condition of the Agreement, including these Policies and Procedures in effect at the time the violation occurred or was discovered; (ii) Violation of any provision in the Compensation Plan; (iii) Violation of any applicable law, ordinance, or regulation affecting EVO Global’s business; or (iv) Engagement in unethical business practices or violation of fair treatment standards. (b) EVO Global will notify the IBO in writing via registered email or mail to the IBO’s last known address regarding EVO Global’s intent to suspend or terminate the IBO’s position and the reasons for suspension or termination. The IBO will have fifteen (15) calendar days from the date of such notice to respond in writing to the allegations or claims constituting grounds for suspension or termination as stated in the notice. EVO Global will then have thirty (30) calendar days from the date of receipt of the IBO’s response to make a final decision regarding suspension or termination. During the notice period, the IBO account will be suspended and will not earn commissions under the Compensation Plan. (c) After the notice period expires, if EVO Global decides to suspend or terminate the IBO’s position, EVO Global will inform the IBO that the position is suspended or terminated as of the notice date. (d) When the severity of allegations against an IBO warrants, EVO Global may expedite or bypass any part of the process outlined in this Section 4.9. (e) If the suspension or termination is not rescinded by EVO Global, the suspension or termination will be effective from the original notice date. The former IBO is prohibited from using the names, trademarks, signs, stationery, advertising, or business materials referring to or associated with any EVO Global service or strategy. EVO Global will notify the active Sponsor within ten (10) days of suspension or termination. Volume associated with the terminated IBO’s sales organization will be permanently "moved" to the next registered active direct Sponsor. (f) An IBO involuntarily terminated by EVO Global may not reapply for a position, whether under their current name or any other name or entity, without the express written consent of an EVO Global officer, following review by the EVO Global Compliance Team. In any event, such IBO may not reapply for a position for twelve (12) months from the termination date.';

$Politics_05 ='5.0 BUSINESS ENTITIES';
$Politics_05_01 ='5.1 Definition';
$Politics_05_01_text ='(a) A corporation or partnership (collectively referred to as "Business Entity") may apply to become an IBO. (b) An IBO may change their status under the same Sponsor from an individual to a partnership or corporation, or from one type of Business Entity to another.';

$Politics_05_02 ='5.2 Independent Business Relationship; Indemnification for Actions';
$Politics_05_02_text ='(a) IBOs are independent contractors acting as fully independent marketing representatives who establish and serve retail customers for EVO Global services and strategies. IBO status does not constitute the sale of a security, franchise, or distributorship, and no IBO fees have been or will be required for the right to market and sell EVO Global services or strategies under the IBO Agreement, other than the IBO monthly administrative fee. The IBO Agreement does not create an employer-employee relationship, agency, partnership, or joint venture between the IBO and any other participant in the EVO Global Compensation Plan and/or EVO Global. (b) IBOs have no authority to bind EVO Global to any obligation. IBOs are responsible for setting their own schedules and supplying all their own equipment and tools to operate their EVO Global business. IBOs will be fully responsible for all applicable federal, state, and local taxes, workers’ compensation contributions, licensing requirements, and fees related to their earnings and activities as an IBO. (c) IBOs will indemnify and hold harmless EVO Global, its directors, officers, employees, contractors, suppliers, and agents from any liability incurred by EVO Global as a result of unauthorized representations or actions by the IBO.';

$Politics_05_03 ='5.3 Insurance';
$Politics_05_03_text ='EVO Global encourages IBOs to arrange insurance coverage for their business. A standard owner’s insurance policy typically does not cover business-related injuries or theft or damage to business inventory or equipment.';

    //-------------------------//

$Politics_06 ='6.0 POLICY VIOLATIONS';
$Politics_06_01 ='6.1 Reporting Policy Violations';
$Politics_06_01_text ='IBOs must email the EVO Global Compliance Team at support@evoglobal.online to report any policy violations by another IBO associated with EVO Global.';

$Politics_06_02 ='6.2 Adherence to the EVO Global Compensation Plan';
$Politics_06_02_text ='(a) IBOs must adhere to the terms of the EVO Global Compensation Plan as set forth in the Agreement and official EVO Global literature. Deviation from the Compensation Plan is prohibited. (b) IBOs may not offer EVO Global opportunities through, or in combination with, any other system, program, or marketing method not specified in official EVO Global literature. (c) IBOs may not require or encourage a current or potential IBO to participate in EVO Global in any way that differs from the Agreement and official EVO Global literature. (d) IBOs may not require or encourage a current or potential IBO to make a purchase or payment to any individual or entity as a condition to participate in the EVO Global Compensation Plan.';

$Politics_06_03 ='6.3 Compliance with Laws and Ordinances';
$Politics_06_03_text ='(a) IBOs must obey local laws regulating home-based businesses. (b) An IBO or Client must comply with all laws related to the operation of their EVO Global business. (c) IBOs and Clients accept sole responsibility for any violation of laws, regulations, or ordinances.';

$Politics_06_04 ='6.4 Compliance with Applicable Income Tax Laws';
$Politics_06_04_text ='(a) An IBO accepts sole responsibility for paying all taxes on any income generated as an EVO Global IBO. (b) IBOs must provide EVO Global with their federal Tax Identification Number or other tax identifier. (c) EVO Global encourages all IBOs to consult a tax advisor for additional guidance regarding their business.';

$Politics_06_05 ='6.5 One EVO Global Business per IBO';
$Politics_06_05_text ='An IBO may operate or have an ownership interest in only one (1) EVO Global business unless expressly authorized by EVO Global. Each position must be built separately and independently from any other.';

$Politics_06_06 ='6.6 Household Members or Affiliate Actions';
$Politics_06_06_text ='If any immediate household member of an IBO engages in any activity that would violate any provision of the Agreement, such activity will be considered a violation by the IBO, and EVO Global may take disciplinary action against the IBO.';

$Politics_06_07 ='6.7 Identification Numbers and Payment';
$Politics_06_07_text ='(a) EVO Global pays commissions only to an e-wallet account in the name of the IBO. The e-wallet account is provided by a third-party provider, and the IBO’s use of the e-wallet is subject to the third-party provider’s terms and conditions. (b) Each IBO is required to provide their federal Social Security Number or Federal Tax Identification Number to EVO Global when initiating a transfer of money or earnings to the IBO e-wallet. (c) Upon enrollment, EVO Global will provide an Identification Number to the IBO.';

$Politics_06_08 ='6.8 Selling, Assigning, or Delegating Ownership';
$Politics_06_08_text ='(a) EVO Global imposes restrictions on the transfer, assignment, or sale of a position to preserve the integrity of the hierarchical structure. (b) An IBO may not sell or assign their rights or delegate their position as an IBO without prior written approval from EVO Global. (c) If the sale is approved by EVO Global, the purchaser assumes the seller’s position and acquires the seller’s downline. (d) To request authorization for a sale or transfer of an EVO Global position, the following items must be submitted to the EVO Global Compliance Team: (i) A duly completed Sale or Transfer Form; (ii) A certified or notarized copy of the executed sale agreement; (iii) A completed and signed IBO Agreement by the Buyer and proof of good standing; (iv) Payment by the seller of the $250 USD administrative fee; (v) Any additional supporting documentation requested by EVO Global. (e) An IBO who sells their position is not eligible to re-enroll as an IBO in any EVO Global sales organization for six (6) full calendar months following the sale date.';

$Politics_06_09 ='6.9 Separating an EVO Global Business';
$Politics_06_09_text ='(a) During a divorce or dissolution of a partnership or other Business Entity, the parties must adopt one of the following methods of operation: (i) One party may, with written consent of the other(s), operate the EVO Global business, whereby the relinquishing spouse, shareholder, partner, or member authorizes EVO Global to deal directly and solely with the non-relinquishing spouse, shareholder, partner, or member. (ii) The parties may continue operating the EVO Global business jointly on a "business as usual" basis, in which case all compensation paid by EVO Global will be paid in the name designated as IBO or in the name of the entity to be divided, as independently agreed upon by the parties. (b) EVO Global recognizes only one sales organization per IBO, and EVO Global will issue only one commission payment per EVO Global business per commission cycle. Under no circumstances will a hierarchy be split, nor will EVO Global split commissions and/or bonuses. (c) If a relinquishing spouse, partner, or business owner has completely relinquished all rights to the original EVO Global business, they may immediately re-enroll under the Sponsor and Placement of their choice.';

$Politics_06_10 ='6.10 Succession';
$Politics_06_10_text ='(a) The Agreement shall be binding and inure to the benefit of the parties and their respective successors and assigns. (b) Upon the death or incapacity of an IBO, the IBO’s business may pass to their legal successors (the "Successor"). The Successor must: (i) Provide evidence of the right to assume the position; (ii) Complete and sign a new Agreement; (iii) Comply with the terms and conditions of the Agreement; (iv) Meet all qualifications for the last rank achieved by the former IBO. (c) Bonuses and commissions of an EVO Global business transferred under this section will be paid in a single transfer to the Successor. The Successor must establish an e-wallet account to which all bonus and commission payments will be sent. (d) If the business is tied to multiple beneficiaries ("Successors"), they must form a Business Entity and obtain a federal business number. EVO Global will issue all bonus and commission payments only to the managing Business Entity. (e) Proper legal documentation must be submitted to the EVO Global Compliance Team to ensure the transfer is executed correctly. (f) To complete a transfer of the EVO Global business due to incapacity, the Successor must provide the following to the EVO Global Compliance Team: (i) A notarized copy of documentation establishing the Successor’s right to manage the EVO Global business; (ii) A completed and executed IBO Agreement by the Successor. (g) If the Successor is already an existing IBO, EVO Global will allow the IBO to maintain their own position plus the inherited active position for up to six (6) months. (h) If the Successor wishes to terminate the EVO Global position, the Successor must submit a notarized statement expressing the desire to terminate the position, along with appropriate legal documentation. (i) Upon written request, EVO Global may grant a one (1) month mourning exemption and pay the Successor at the last "paid as" rank.';

    //-------------------------//

$Politics_07 ='7.0 DISCIPLINARY ACTIONS';
$Politics_07_01 ='7.1 Imposition of Disciplinary Action';
$Politics_07_01_text ='Purpose: EVO Global believes that integrity and fairness must prevail among its IBOs, providing everyone an equal opportunity to build a successful business. Therefore, EVO Global reserves the right to impose disciplinary sanctions at any time when it has determined that an IBO has violated the Agreement, including these Policies and Procedures, as may be amended from time to time by EVO Global.';

$Politics_07_02 ='7.2 Consequences and Remedies for Non-Compliance';
$Politics_07_02_text ='Disciplinary actions for non-compliance with the Agreement may include one or more of the following: (i) Advising the IBO regarding compliance; (ii) Monitoring the IBO’s conduct to ensure compliance; (iii) Issuing a warning or requiring the IBO to take immediate corrective actions; (iv) Imposing a fine or withholding commission payments until the matter causing the Commission Hold is resolved or until EVO Global receives adequate additional assurances from the IBO to ensure future compliance; (v) Suspension from participation in EVO Global events, rewards, or recognition; (vi) Suspension of the IBO’s position for one or more pay periods; (vii) Involuntary termination of the IBO Agreement and position; (viii) Any other action EVO Global deems feasible and appropriate to justly resolve damages caused by the Policy violation or IBO’s contractual non-compliance; (ix) Legal proceedings for monetary or equitable relief.';

$Politics_07_03 ='7.3 Suspension Procedures';
$Politics_07_03_text ='(a) EVO Global may, but is not required to, follow the following suspension procedures (the "Disciplinary Policy"): (b) First Violation: Counseling and initial warning. (i) A first violation may occur because the IBO is not familiar with the Agreement or IBO obligations. Counseling and the initial warning provide an opportunity for the EVO Global Compliance Team to draw the IBO’s attention to the Agreement and the specific violation, and provide guidance on compliance. (c) Second Violation: Second warning and temporary suspension. (i) The second warning may indicate the severity of repeated violations and may result in a temporary suspension of the IBO account. During the suspension period, the IBO forfeits all rights to Payments. (d) Third Violation: Termination. (i) EVO Global will attempt to exercise the progressive nature of the Disciplinary Policy by first providing warnings, a final warning, and suspension and loss of commissions before proceeding to termination; however, EVO Global reserves the right to combine and omit steps depending on the circumstances of each situation and the nature of the violation. (e) Serious Violations (i) EVO Global treats the posting of non-compliant content on social media as a serious violation of the Agreement and will accelerate the disciplinary process for such violations.';

$Politics_08 ='8.0 DISPUTE RESOLUTION';
$Politics_08_01 = '8.1 Complaints Between IBOs';
$Politics_08_01_text = '(a) If an IBO has a complaint or claim against another IBO regarding any practice or conduct related to their respective EVO Global businesses, they are encouraged to resolve the issue directly with the other party. If a resolution cannot be reached, it must be reported directly to the EVO Global Compliance Team as described in this Section. (b) The EVO Global Compliance Team shall be the final authority to resolve any complaints or claims between IBOs on matters related to the EVO Global business, and its decision shall be final and binding on all IBOs. (c) EVO Global will limit its intervention to disputes related solely to EVO Global business matters. EVO Global will not decide issues involving personality conflicts or unprofessional conduct by or between IBOs outside the context of an EVO Global business. These matters are beyond the scope of EVO Global and cannot be used to justify a Sponsor or Placement change or a transfer to another EVO Global organization. (d) EVO Global does not consider, enforce, or mediate third-party agreements between IBOs, nor provide names, funds, or advice to obtain external legal counsel. (e) Complaint Process: (i) The IBO must submit a complaint letter (email accepted) directly to the EVO Global Compliance Team at support@evoglobal.online. The letter must outline the details of the incident as follows: (A) Nature of the violation; (B) Specific facts supporting the allegations; (C) Dates; (D) Number of occurrences; (E) People involved; and (F) Supporting documentation. (ii) Upon receiving the written complaint, EVO Global may conduct an investigation according to the following procedures: (A) The EVO Global Compliance Team may send an acknowledgment to the complaining IBO; (B) The EVO Global Compliance Team may provide verbal or written notice of the allegation to the IBO under investigation. If written notice is sent to the IBO, the IBO will have ten (10) business days from the date of the notification letter to submit all information related to the incident for review by EVO Global. (C) The EVO Global Compliance Team will investigate the complaint and consider any information presented that it deems relevant, including information from collateral sources. Due to the unique nature of each situation, determinations of appropriate remedies will be made on a case-by-case basis, and the time to reach a resolution will vary. (D) During the investigation, the EVO Global Compliance Team may provide only periodic updates simply indicating that the investigation is ongoing. No other information will be released during this time. Calls, letters, and requests for progress reports from IBOs during the investigation will not be returned. (E) EVO Global will make a final decision and promptly notify the IBOs involved.';

$Politics_08_02 = '8.2 Dispute Resolution';
$Politics_08_02_text = 'PLEASE READ THIS SECTION OF THE IBO AGREEMENT CAREFULLY, AS IT PROVIDES THE RESOLUTION OF MOST DISPUTES THROUGH BINDING ARBITRATION AND INCLUDES CERTAIN WAIVERS, INCLUDING CLASS ACTION, CLASS ARBITRATION, AND JURY TRIAL WAIVERS.

(a) IBOs, Clients, and EVO Global (for the purposes of this section, collectively "the Parties") acknowledge that disputes and differences may arise among the Parties and therefore agree it is in their interest to appoint an impartial mediator to resolve such disputes as they arise. 
(b) All disputes and claims relating to EVO Global, a primarily online company offering digital services, the IBO Agreement, or EVO Global services and strategies, the rights and obligations of an IBO and EVO Global, or any other claim or cause of action relating to the performance of an IBO and EVO Global under the Agreement ("Dispute") shall be fully and finally resolved by arbitration. Although Evo Movement International S.A. de C.V. is registered in Mexico and the primary arbitration venue shall be Cancún, Mexico, EVO Global operates internationally, and arbitration locations may be adjusted to accommodate international disputes, or anywhere else prescribed by EVO Global, in accordance with applicable international arbitration rules and Mexican law. All parties will have discovery rights allowed under applicable law, subject to all limitations contained therein. The arbitrator’s decision will be final and binding on the parties and, if necessary, may be entered as a judgment in any court of competent jurisdiction. Each party in arbitration shall be responsible for its own costs and expenses of arbitration, including legal and filing fees. Nothing in the Agreement shall prevent EVO Global from seeking and obtaining from any court with jurisdiction a writ of attachment, temporary, preliminary, permanent injunction, or other available relief to safeguard and protect EVO Global’s interests before, during, or after any arbitration or other proceeding pending the rendering of a decision or award in connection with any arbitration or other proceedings. Arbitration proceedings and any award shall remain confidential. No amendment to this arbitration provision shall apply to a Dispute of which EVO Global had actual knowledge as of the date of the amendment. Any termination of this arbitration provision shall not be effective until ten (10) days after reasonable notice of termination is provided to IBOs or as to Disputes arising prior to the termination date. (c) CLASS ACTION WAIVER. IN THE EVENT ANY DISPUTE PROCEEDS IN COURT RATHER THAN THROUGH ARBITRATION, FOR ANY REASON, EACH IBO AND EVO GLOBAL AGREE THAT SUCH DISPUTE SHALL BE RESOLVED SOLELY ON AN INDIVIDUAL BASIS. EACH IBO AND EVO GLOBAL SPECIFICALLY AGREE THAT CLAIMS MAY BE BROUGHT AGAINST THE OTHER ONLY IN THEIR INDIVIDUAL CAPACITY, AND NOT AS A PLAINTIFF OR CLASS MEMBER IN ANY PURPORTED CLASS, COLLECTIVE, REPRESENTATIVE, OR GROUP ACTION. (d) JURY TRIAL WAIVER. TO THE EXTENT ANY DISPUTE PROCEEDS IN COURT RATHER THAN THROUGH ARBITRATION, FOR ANY REASON, IF NOT PROHIBITED BY APPLICABLE LAW, EACH IBO AND EVO GLOBAL HEREBY WAIVE ANY RIGHT TO A JURY TRIAL TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW. (e) Delegation to Arbitrator. Except as provided in this Section 9, I acknowledge and agree that the arbitrator(s), and not any federal, state, or local court, shall have exclusive authority to resolve any Dispute relating to the interpretation, applicability, enforceability, or validity of these Dispute Resolution Provisions, including, without limitation, any claim that these Dispute Resolution Provisions are void or voidable. (f) Severability. If any provision contained in these Dispute Resolution Provisions is found to be invalid or unenforceable, such provision shall be automatically modified to the minimum extent necessary to render the parties’ agreement to arbitrate valid and enforceable. If a provision conflicts with a mandatory provision of applicable law, the conflicting provision shall automatically be severed, and the remainder shall be construed to incorporate the mandatory provision. In the event of such severance or modification, the remainder shall not be affected. (g) Survival. The Dispute Resolution Provisions shall remain in effect even after termination of the Agreement or termination of the IBO’s business association with EVO Global.';

$Politics_08_03 ='8.3 Severability';
$Politics_08_03_text = 'If any provision of the Agreement is found to be invalid or unenforceable for any reason, only the invalid provision shall be excluded. The remaining terms and provisions shall remain in full force and effect and shall be construed as if such invalid or unenforceable provision had never been part of the Agreement.';

$Politics_08_04 ='8.4 Waiver';
$Politics_08_04_text = '(a) Only an officer of EVO Global may, in writing, effect a waiver of the Agreement. (b) EVO Global\'s waiver of any particular breach by an IBO shall not affect EVO Global\'s rights with respect to any subsequent breach, nor affect the rights or obligations of any other IBO. (c) The existence of any claim or cause of action by an IBO against EVO Global shall not constitute a defense to EVO Global\'s enforcement of any term or provision of the Agreement.';

$Politics_08_05 ='8.5 Governing Law';
$Politics_08_05_text = 'Subject to and without waiving the foregoing terms, the jurisdiction and venue for any controversy or claim arising out of the Agreement or between EVO Global and the IBO shall be in Cancún, Mexico, where the corporate office of Evo Movement International S.A. de C.V. is located. The laws of Mexico shall govern all matters related to or arising from the Agreement or between EVO Global and IBOs, considering the global and online nature of services provided by EVO Global.';

$Politics_09 = '9.0 Payment of Commissions and Bonuses';
$Politics_09_text = '';

$Politics_09_01 = '9.1 Bonus and Commission Qualifications';
$Politics_09_01_text = '(a) An IBO must be active and in compliance with the Agreement to qualify for commissions. As long as an IBO complies with the terms and conditions set forth in the Agreement, EVO Global will pay commissions to such IBOs in accordance with this Agreement, the Compensation Plan, and any amendments thereto. (b) EVO Global will not issue any payment in any form to an IBO without first receiving all administrative fees and a completed electronic EVO Global request, including an executed copy of this Agreement. (c) EVO Global reserves the right to defer commission payments until the accumulated amount of bonuses and commissions owed to an IBO exceeds $50.00.';

$Politics_09_02 = '9.2 Calculation of Commissions and Discrepancies';
$Politics_09_02_text = '(a) Commissions, bonuses, override commissions, and achievement levels are calculated monthly. (b) An IBO must review their earnings statement in their virtual office immediately and report any discrepancy within thirty (30) days of receiving a commission payment. Requests submitted after thirty (30) days will not be considered. (c) For additional information regarding commission payments, refer to the Compensation Plan.';

$Politics_09_03 = '9.3 Adjustments to Bonuses and Commissions for Returned IBO Services or Memberships';
$Politics_09_03_text = '(a) An IBO earns commissions based on actual sales of services and strategies to Clients through purchases of services and strategies. When services or strategies are canceled by a Client and EVO Global issues a refund to the Client, commissions attributable to the refunded service will be deducted from the IBO who received commissions for those sales. Deductions will occur in the month the refund is granted and will continue each pay period until the commission is recovered. (b) In the event an IBO terminates their position, and the bonus or commission amounts attributable to refunded services or strategies have not been fully recovered by EVO Global, the remaining balance may be offset against any other amount EVO Global may owe the terminated IBO.';

$Politics_10 = '10.0 Service Order Policies';
$Politics_10_text = '';

$Politics_10_01 = '10.1 General Service Order Policies';
$Politics_10_01_text = '(a) "Bonus Buying" is strictly and absolutely prohibited. Bonus Buying includes: (a) enrolling individuals or Business Entities without their knowledge and/or completion of online enrollment by such individuals or Business Entities; (b) fraudulent enrollment of an individual or Business Entity as an IBO or Client; (c) enrolling or attempting to enroll non-existent individuals or Business Entities as IBOs or Clients ("ghosts"); (d) purchasing EVO Global services or strategies on behalf of another IBO or Client, or under another IBO or Client ID number, to qualify for commissions or bonuses; and/or (e) any other mechanism or artifice to qualify for rank advancement, incentives, awards, commissions, or bonuses that is not driven by genuine consumer purchases of services or strategies. (b) EVO Global requires IBOs to use their own payment method and not allow others to use it. An IBO must not use another IBO or Client’s credit card or debit account to enroll in EVO Global or purchase services without the account holder’s written permission. (c) When an IBO’s payment method is invalid or cannot be processed, EVO Global will attempt to contact the IBO by phone, mail, or email to obtain another form of payment. If these attempts fail, any service order related to the invalid payment method may be canceled. (d) Prices are subject to change without notice. (e) Any error or incorrect charge to an IBO payment method must be reported to EVO Global within three (3) calendar days of the transaction date.';

$Politics_10_02 = '10.2 Sales to Clients';
$Politics_10_02_text = '(a) Sales to Clients must be made directly through the IBO’s replicated website. (b) IBOs must comply with applicable consumer protection laws and regulations (including any consumer rights to receive specific notices and any right to return services) granted to consumers.';

$Politics_10_03 = '10.3 Insufficient Funds';
$Politics_10_03_text = '(a) All electronic payments rejected for insufficient funds will be automatically resubmitted for payment. (b) Any outstanding balance an IBO owes EVO Global for NSF (non-sufficient funds) or NSF fees (ACH) will be withheld by EVO Global from future bonuses and commissions of that IBO. (c) All insufficient fund transactions not timely resolved by the IBO constitute grounds for disciplinary action or account termination. (d) If a credit or debit card order is declined the first time, the IBO will be contacted directly to provide an alternative payment method. If these attempts fail, any service order related to the invalid payment method may be canceled.';

$Politics_10_04 = '10.4 Credit Card Purchases';
$Politics_10_04_text = '(a) Credit card purchases may only be made by the person whose name and address appear on the credit card. Any IBO using another person’s credit card to pay for purchases risks suspension of their EVO Global account pending investigation and resolution of any complaints regarding unauthorized charges. EVO Global considers such transactions fraudulent and will report them to the appropriate authorities. (b) Under no circumstances may an IBO unreasonably reverse any credit card purchase. If an IBO reverses any payment to EVO Global, that IBO will immediately lose all credit card ordering privileges until disputed charges are resolved. If it is determined that the disputed charges are valid and/or the reversal is deemed unreasonable and/or unjustified, EVO Global may terminate the IBO’s position. If an erroneous charge is applied to an IBO’s credit card, the IBO must immediately contact the EVO Global Support Team by email at support@evoglobal.online to initiate an investigation and resolution.';

$Politics_10_05 = '10.5 Sales Tax Obligation';
$Politics_10_05_text = '(a) The IBO must comply with all federal and local taxes and regulations governing the sale of EVO Global services or strategies. (b) EVO Global encourages each IBO to consult with a tax advisor for additional information for their business. (c) EVO Global may be required to collect and remit sales tax to various states and countries based on the retail sale price of services.';

$Politics_10_06 = '10.6 Refund Policy';
$Politics_10_06_text = 'EVO Global Clients: (i) If within the first seven (7) days a Client is not satisfied with the service, they must contact support@evoglobal.online for a full refund of amounts paid to EVO Global, except for Bitcoin purchases. (ii) All purchases are charged and refunded in United States Dollars. All refunds and exchanges will be processed using the original payment method and refunded or exchanged in United States Dollars. EVO Global is not responsible for any loss due to fluctuations in exchange rates.';

$Politics_11 = '11.0 EVO Global OPPORTUNITY';
$Politics_11_text = '';

$Politics_11_01 = '11.1 Presentation of the Compensation Plan';
$Politics_11_01_text = 'Income Claims When presenting the EVO Global opportunity to prospective IBOs, an IBO must comply with the following provisions: (i) An IBO must not misrepresent or omit any material fact regarding the Compensation Plan. (ii) An IBO must make clear that the Compensation Plan is based on EVO Global service sales and not on sponsoring other IBOs. (iii) An IBO must make clear that success can only be achieved through substantial and diligent independent effort. (iv) An IBO must not make income projections, claims, or guarantees when presenting or discussing the EVO Global opportunity or the Compensation Plan to prospective IBOs. All prospective IBOs must be informed that success requires substantial work. Income claims include, but are not limited to, copies of paychecks, bank statements, rank earnings, tax documents, trading profits, lifestyle claims, or photos (e.g., cash, exotic cars, yachts, etc.). Income claims are prohibited at events and/or on social media posts, websites, or videos. If an IBO is found to have posted income or lifestyle claims on social media, they will receive a notice to remove the post immediately. Failure to remove a post upon request may result in suspension. Repeat offenses may result in suspension or possible termination. (v) An IBO may not make any income or earnings claims or show trading results based on or with respect to EVO Global services or strategies. (vi) An IBO may not recommend or be affiliated with brokers or investment advisors nor make any claim that EVO Global is offering products or services other than a platform and educational services. (vii) An IBO may not claim or imply that the EVO Global opportunity or Compensation Plan can replace or exceed income impacted by Coronavirus Disease 2019 (COVID-19).';

$Politics_11_02 = '11.2 Events';
$Politics_11_02_text = '(a) IBOs are limited to charging a reasonable per-person seat fee for events to cover venue rental and associated event costs. (b) All marketing materials created by an IBO to support an IBO event and all stage content must comply with the Agreement, including these Policies and Procedures, and all applicable laws and regulations.';

$Politics_11_03 = '11.3 Trading Policies';
$Politics_11_03_text = '(a) IBOs are strictly prohibited from selling Signals, Trading Bots, Auto-traders, or receiving investments to trade. Any violation will result in immediate termination. (b) Trading challenges or projected growth charts are prohibited.';

$Politics_11_04 = '11.4 Sales Requirements Governed by the Compensation Plan';
$Politics_11_04_text = 'No exclusive territories are granted to anyone. Franchise fees do not apply to an EVO Global business.';

$Politics_12 = '12.0 PROPRIETARY INFORMATION AND TRADE SECRETS';
$Politics_12_text = '';

$Politics_12_01 = '12.1 Business Reports, Lists, and Proprietary Information';
$Politics_12_01_text = 'By accepting the Agreement, IBOs and Clients acknowledge that business reports, the identity and contact information of Clients, IBOs, and prospective Clients or IBOs (including that available in group chats), information about the genealogy of EVO Global or an IBO, and any other financial, technical, or other information that is not generally known and/or is sensitive in nature and circulated by EVO Global or owned by EVO Global’s business, whether written or otherwise, whether received directly from EVO Global or from other IBOs, are confidential and proprietary information and trade secrets belonging to Evo Movement International S.A. de C.V.';

$Politics_12_02 = '12.2 Duty of Confidentiality';
$Politics_12_02_text = 'IBOs must not use Evo Movement International S.A. de C.V.’s Confidential Information and Trade Secrets for any purpose other than promoting an IBO’s EVO Global business. An IBO may never disclose Evo Movement International S.A. de C.V.’s non-public Confidential Information and Trade Secrets to anyone outside EVO Global without EVO Global management’s written consent.';

$Politics_12_03 = '12.3 Breach and Remedies';
$Politics_12_03_text = 'IBOs acknowledge that EVO Global’s non-public Confidential Information and Trade Secrets are of such a nature that they are unique, and that disclosure or use in violation of §12.1 et seq. will result in immediate and irreparable harm to EVO Global and EVO Global’s IBO business. In addition to recovering any damages, EVO Global and its IBOs shall be entitled to expedited injunctive relief against any IBO violating this provision in any action to enforce its rights under this section. EVO Global may seek such expedited injunctive relief under applicable international and Mexican laws. The prevailing party shall be entitled to an award of attorney’s fees, court costs, and expenses.';

$Politics_12_04 = '12.4 Return of Materials';
$Politics_12_04_text = 'An IBO must immediately return to EVO Global the original and all copies of all EVO Global Confidential Information and Trade Secrets in their possession upon (1) termination of this Agreement, or (2) demand by EVO Global.';

$Politics_13 = '13.0 PRIVACY POLICY';
$Politics_13_text = '';

$Politics_13_01 = '13.1 Introduction';
$Politics_13_01_text = 'All IBOs must understand and adhere to the basic principles of confidentiality and data privacy, and their use of the EVO Global website is subject to the terms of EVO Global’s Privacy Policy (“Privacy Policy”) posted on the evo.global website, as amended from time to time. Without limiting the terms of this section, all IBOs must comply with applicable privacy laws governing the collection, use, and disclosure of Client and fellow IBO information.';

$Politics_13_02 = '13.2 Expectation of Privacy';
$Politics_13_02_text = '(a) EVO Global recognizes and respects the importance Clients and IBOs place on the privacy of their financial and personal information. EVO Global will safeguard privacy and maintain the confidentiality of Clients’ and IBOs’ financial and account information and non-public personal information in accordance with its Privacy Policy. (b) By entering into the Agreement, an IBO authorizes EVO Global to disclose their name and contact information to Upline IBOs solely for activities related to promoting the EVO Global business. An IBO agrees to maintain the confidentiality and security of such information and to use it only to support and service their downline organization and conduct the EVO Global business.';

$Politics_13_03 = '13.3 Restrictions on Account Information Disclosure';
$Politics_13_03_text = 'EVO Global will not share non-public personal or financial information about current or former Clients or IBOs with third parties, except in accordance with the Agreement, the Privacy Policy, as permitted or required by laws and regulations, court orders, or to serve the interests of Clients, or IBOs, or to enforce rights or obligations under the Agreement, or with the written permission of the registered account holder.';

$Politics_14 = '14.0 ADVERTISING, PROMOTIONAL MATERIALS, USE OF COMPANY NAMES AND TRADEMARKS';
$Politics_14_text = '';

$Politics_14_01 = '14.1 Display of Services';
$Politics_14_01_text = '(a) An IBO may not rebrand electronically or otherwise any EVO Global service, strategy, information, material, or program in any way. EVO Global services and strategies must only be sold through EVO Global replicated website ecosystem hosted on EVO Global servers. (b) An IBO must not have any EVO Global service, strategy, or trade name promoted, sold, or displayed at retail establishments except where the retail establishment is owned or operated by the IBO and the establishment does not exceed $1 million in annual gross revenue, and there are five (5) or fewer establishments under common ownership or operation. (c) An IBO may sell EVO Global services or strategies and display the EVO Global trade name at any appropriate trade show booth (e.g., trade shows, exhibitions, conferences, etc.) with EVO Global’s express written consent subject to the following. (i) An IBO is prohibited from selling EVO Global services or strategies or displaying the trade name, trademark, or service mark of EVO Global in any kiosk or booth located in any retail establishment, including, without limitation, a mall or retail facility. (ii) EVO Global reserves the right, in its sole discretion, to refuse authorization for an IBO to participate in any function EVO Global does not consider a suitable forum for promoting EVO Global services and strategies, or the EVO Global business opportunity.';

$Politics_14_02 = '14.2 Use of Company Names and Protected Materials';
$Politics_14_02_text = '(a) An IBO must safeguard and promote the good reputation of Evo Global and the services they market. Marketing and promotion of Evo Global, its services, the Evo Global business opportunity, and the Compensation Plan must be consistent with public interest and avoid any rude, misleading, confusing, unethical, or immoral conduct and practices. (b) All promotional materials provided or created by Evo Global must be used in their original form and may not be changed, modified, or altered, except with prior written approval from the Evo Global Compliance Team. (c) The name Evo Global, each of its service names, and other names adopted by Evo Global in connection with its business are trade names, registered trademarks, and service marks owned by Evo Global. As such, these marks are of significant value to Evo Global and are provided to IBOs for use only in a manner expressly authorized. (d) The use of the name “Evo Global” is restricted to protect Evo Global’s proprietary rights and ensure that Evo Global’s protected names are not lost or compromised by unauthorized use. The use of the Evo Global name in connection with any product, service, or strategy not produced or offered by Evo Global is prohibited except as follows: (i) [IBO Name] Independent IBO of Evo Global or Independent Business Owner of Evo Global. (ii) [IBO Name] Independent IBO of Evo Global Services. (e) Additional restrictions on using the Evo Global name include: (i) Any stationery bearing the Evo Global name or logo intended for use by the IBO must be emailed to the Evo Global Compliance Team for approval at support@evoglobal.online. (ii) IBOs may list “Independent IBO of Evo Global Academy” in white pages or equivalent online directories under their own name. (iii) IBOs may not use the Evo Global name when answering phones, creating an outgoing voicemail message, or using an answering service in such a way that gives the caller the impression of contacting Evo Global corporate office. IBOs may answer calls describing themselves as an “Independent IBO of Evo Global” or Independent Distributor of Evo Global. (f) Certain photos and graphics used by Evo Global in advertising, packaging, and websites result from paid contracts with third parties and do not extend to IBOs. If an IBO wants to use such materials, they must negotiate individual contracts with third parties for a fee. (g) An IBO must not promote non-Evo Global services, strategies, or products together with Evo Global services or strategies on the same social media site or ad without prior approval from the Evo Global Compliance Team. (h) IBOs may not make claims, including personal testimonials, related to any service or strategy offered by Evo Global, except as contained in official Evo Global literature. To avoid doubt, IBOs are prohibited from making any claim that Evo Global services or strategies, or the Evo Global business opportunity, guarantee financial growth or investment returns, profits, or any other statement that could be understood as an investment return guarantee.';

$Politics_14_03 = '14.3 Faxes and Email – Limitations';
$Politics_14_03_text ='(a) Except as provided in this section, an IBO may not use or transmit unsolicited email, mass email distribution, other commercial electronic messages, or “spam” promoting or advertising their Evo Global business. Exceptions are: (i) Sending emails to anyone who has given prior permission or invitation; and/or (ii) Sending emails to anyone with whom the IBO has an existing business or personal relationship. (b) In all U.S. states or territories or international locations where prohibited by law, an IBO may not transmit, or cause to be transmitted through a third party (by phone, fax, computer, or other device), an unsolicited advertisement to any equipment capable of transcribing text or images from an electronic signal received over a regular phone line, cable line, ISDN, T1, or any other signaling device, except as set forth in this section. (c) All email or computer-transmitted documents subject to this provision must include the following: (i) Clear identification that the fax or email is an advertisement or solicitation. The words “advertisement” or “solicitation” must appear in the subject line of the message; (ii) A clear return path or routing information; (iii) Use of a legally valid and correct domain name; (iv) A clear and conspicuous notice of the opportunity to opt-out of receiving further fax or commercial email messages from the sender; (v) Instructions to unsubscribe or opt-out must appear as the first text in the body in the same font size as the majority of the message; (vi) The true and correct name of the sender, valid fax of sender, or email address, and a valid physical address of the sender; (vii) Date and time of transmission; (viii) After notice from the recipient requesting no further fax or email messages, an IBO must not transmit further documents to that recipient. (d) All email or computer-transmitted documents must not include: (i) Use of any third-party domain without permission; or (ii) Explicitly sexual material.';

$Politics_14_05 = '14.5 Advertising and Promotional Materials';
$Politics_14_05_text ='Advertising and all forms of communication must adhere to principles of honesty and ownership.';

$Politics_14_06 = '14.6 Permission for Testimonials';
$Politics_14_06_text ='Evo Global may use, without compensation, an IBO’s testimonial or likeness in all corporate sales materials, including, but not limited to, print media, electronic media, audio, and video. As consideration for being allowed to participate in the Evo Global business opportunity, an IBO waives any right to be compensated for the use of their testimonial or likeness even if Evo Global is paid for sales materials containing such likeness, and represents that any testimonial represents the IBO’s current, original, and honest opinions, thoughts, beliefs, findings, or experiences based on the IBO’s real experience with Evo Global and any declared use of Evo Global services and/or strategies. IBOs agree to notify Evo Global immediately of any change in the views expressed in the testimonial. In some cases, an IBO’s testimonial may appear in another IBO’s promotional materials.';

$Politics_14_07 = '14.7 Telemarketing – Limitations';
$Politics_14_07_text ='(a) An IBO must not engage in telemarketing in connection with any work performed for or related to Evo Global in violation of applicable laws, regulations, and codes. “Telemarketing” means making one or more telephone calls or fax transmissions to individuals or entities to induce them to purchase Evo Global services or strategies or to recruit them for the Evo Global opportunity. (b) The U.S. federal government administers the Unsolicited Telecommunications Rules and operates a national Do Not Call registry requiring businesses to refrain from calling numbers listed on a “Do Not Call” list (DNCL) and/or individuals who directly tell the caller not to call/fax in the future. (c) Even if an IBO may not consider themselves a “telemarketer,” regulations broadly define “telemarketer” and “telemarketing,” so the unintentional act of calling someone listed in a Do Not Call registry could violate the law. These regulations carry significant penalties. (d) “Cold calls” or unsolicited calls/faxes to prospective Clients or IBOs to promote Evo Global services, strategies, or business opportunity are considered telemarketing and are prohibited. (e) An IBO may not use automatic dialing systems in operating their Evo Global business. (f) Violation of the Agreement or laws, regulations, or codes regarding telemarketing may result in sanctions against the IBO by Evo Global, up to and including termination. (g) By accepting the Agreement or receiving commissions, other payments, or awards from Evo Global, an IBO permits Evo Global and other IBOs to contact them as allowed under federal Do Not Call regulations. (h) If an IBO violates this section, Evo Global reserves the right to institute legal proceedings for monetary or equitable relief. (i) Exceptions to Telemarketing Regulations: An IBO may make calls or faxes to prospective Clients or IBOs under limited circumstances: (i) If the IBO has an established current business relationship with the prospect; (ii) In response to a personal inquiry or request from the prospect regarding a service or strategy offered by the IBO, but only for three (3) months after that inquiry or request; (iii) If the IBO receives written and signed permission from the prospect authorizing calls/faxes; (iv) If the call/fax is to family members, personal friends, and acquaintances. However, if an IBO habitually collects business cards from everyone they meet and later calls or faxes them, the federal government may consider this telemarketing not exempt; (v) IBOs making calls to “acquaintances” must do so occasionally, not as routine practice.';

$Politics_15 = '15.0 INTERNATIONAL MARKETING';
$Politics_15_text = 'Each IBO must comply with all applicable laws and regulations in the country, state, or province where they are marketing Evo Global services, strategies, or business opportunity outside Mexico.';

$Politics_16 = '16.0 EVO GLOBAL TERMS GLOSSARY';
$Politics_16_text = 'ACTIVE IBO: An IBO in good standing under the Agreement and meeting minimum sales volume requirements as set forth in the Compensation Plan. COMPENSATION PLAN: Guidelines and referenced literature describing how IBOs can earn commissions and bonuses. COMPLIANCE TEAM: The Evo Global Compliance Team, contactable at support@evoglobal.online. CLIENT: An end consumer purchasing Evo Global services and not participating in building a business or promoting sales of Evo Global services and strategies. CUSTOMER SERVICE TEAM: Evo Global Customer Service Team, contactable at support@evoglobal.online. DOWNLINE: IBO or IBOs located below another IBO in any Evo Global marketing or sales organization or Genealogy. SPONSOR OR SPONSORING IBO: An IBO who enrolls a Client, retailer, or other IBO with Evo Global and is listed as the Sponsor in the IBO Agreement. The act of enrolling and training others to become IBOs is called “sponsorship.” INDEPENDENT BUSINESS OWNER (“IBO”): An individual or entity actively promoting, marketing, and selling Evo Global services and/or strategies for profit and actively recruiting others to do the same under the Agreement. SPONSOR LINE (“LOS”): A report generated by Evo Global providing critical data regarding IBO identities, sales information, and enrollment activity of each IBO’s organization. This report contains confidential and trade secret information owned by Evo Global. ORGANIZATION or MARKETING NETWORK or GENEALOGY: Clients and IBOs located above or below a particular IBO in the Evo Global marketing and sales structure or genealogy. EVO GLOBAL MATERIALS: Literature, audio or video tapes, and/or any other material developed, printed, published, or distributed by Evo Global, including to IBOs and Clients. LOCATION: The position of an IBO within their Sponsor’s organization. RECRUIT or RECRUITMENT: The solicitation, enrollment, encouragement, or actual or attempted effort to influence another IBO or Client to enroll or participate in a multilevel marketing, network marketing, or direct sales opportunity. SUPPORT TEAM: Evo Global Support Team, contactable at support@evoglobal.online. UPLINE: An IBO or IBOs located above another IBO in any Evo Global marketing network or genealogy.';

